    a: "Linear regression fits a straight line (or plane) y = w*x + b that minimizes the squared error between predictions and real values. The coefficients tell me how much the target changes when a feature increases by one. It is fast and easy to explain, so it is my first baseline for regression, but it assumes a roughly linear relationship.",
