    level: 'Intermediate',
    a: "Naive Bayes uses Bayes' theorem to compute the probability of each class, assuming all features are independent given the class. That assumption is 'naive' and rarely true, but it still works very well for text like spam filtering. It is extremely fast and a great baseline for text classification.",
    code: "from sklearn.feature_extraction.text import CountVectorizer\nfrom sklearn.naive_bayes import MultinomialNB\n\ntexts = [\"win money now\", \"free prize win\", \"meeting at noon\",\n         \"project meeting notes\", \"win a free trip\", \"lunch at noon\"]\nlabels = [\"spam\", \"spam\", \"ham\", \"ham\", \"spam\", \"ham\"]\n\nvec = CountVectorizer()\nX = vec.fit_transform(texts)\nnb = MultinomialNB().fit(X, labels)\n\nfor msg in [\"free money\", \"notes from the meeting\"]:\n    pred = nb.predict(vec.transform([msg]))[0]\n    print(f\"{msg!r} -> {pred}\")",
