    level: 'Intermediate',
    a: "Gradient boosting builds trees one after another, where each new small tree learns to fix the errors of the previous ones. XGBoost, LightGBM and CatBoost are fast, optimized versions of this idea and often win on tabular data. The key settings are n_estimators, learning_rate and max_depth, and I use early stopping to avoid overfitting.",
    code: "from sklearn.datasets import load_breast_cancer\nfrom sklearn.model_selection import train_test_split\nfrom sklearn.ensemble import GradientBoostingClassifier\n\nX, y = load_breast_cancer(return_X_y=True)\nX_tr, X_te, y_tr, y_te = train_test_split(X, y, random_state=0, stratify=y)\n\nfor n in [1, 10, 100]:\n    gb = GradientBoostingClassifier(n_estimators=n, learning_rate=0.1,\n                                    max_depth=3, random_state=0)\n    gb.fit(X_tr, y_tr)\n    print(f\"trees={n:3d}  test accuracy={gb.score(X_te, y_te):.3f}\")",
